DirectInput's explicit Unacquire path removes the device from the acquired
list before refreshing the input thread. The refresh cannot remove that
device's CBT hook once it is no longer in the list. Remove the hook while
holding the same lock that protects hook installation and list membership.

Repeated foreground keyboard/mouse acquisition otherwise exhausts Wine's
hook-chain recursion limit, preventing MFC from attaching newly created
windows (3DMark2001 SE eventually passes a null HWND to DirectInput).

diff --git a/dlls/dinput/dinput_main.c b/dlls/dinput/dinput_main.c
--- a/dlls/dinput/dinput_main.c
+++ b/dlls/dinput/dinput_main.c
@@ -464,3 +464,4 @@ void dinput_hooks_unacquire_device( IDirectInputDevice8W *iface )
     EnterCriticalSection( &dinput_hook_crit );
+    unhook_device_window_foreground_changes( impl );
     list_remove( &impl->entry );
     LeaveCriticalSection( &dinput_hook_crit );
